WEBVTT

00:29.880 --> 00:31.090
Going for the kill?

00:32.390 --> 00:35.720
Against someone
who never bore you any grudge.

00:42.900 --> 00:44.740
Just another person, like you.

03:04.540 --> 03:08.710
In the end, this world is nothing
but an endless feast.

03:09.210 --> 03:11.250
Now, let us dig in!

03:11.250 --> 03:13.130
When negotiating with merchants,

03:13.130 --> 03:15.590
you'd do best to listen until the end.

03:20.430 --> 03:22.890
Because they always have
something up their sleeve.

03:25.470 --> 03:28.310
Water dragons are merciless hunters.

03:39.450 --> 03:41.240
Woah, nice!

03:41.240 --> 03:44.080
Did you do that?

03:44.080 --> 03:47.110
Thank you. You saved us.

03:47.920 --> 03:51.170
I'm not going to pry
on how you controlled them, though.

03:51.670 --> 03:53.960
I'd appreciate that.

03:53.960 --> 03:57.510
So, why are you here, Lady Felt?
What about Mr. Heinkel—

03:57.510 --> 04:01.000
Camberley's watchin'
that wrinkly asswipe.

04:01.000 --> 04:04.140
We were just on our way to pick up
somethin' we left at the inn.

04:04.550 --> 04:07.100
Something you left at the inn?

04:07.100 --> 04:08.350
Yup.

04:08.350 --> 04:12.060
It's a secret weapon
our sorcerer gave me.

04:12.060 --> 04:15.570
It's supposedly a really
powerful meteor—

04:15.570 --> 04:16.320
Just a moment.

04:40.640 --> 04:44.760
Lady Felt, how reliable
is that meteor you mentioned?

04:44.760 --> 04:50.100
According to Old Man Rom and the rest,
even Reinhard wouldn't come out unscathed.

04:50.100 --> 04:53.800
Haha.
That metric sure is easy to grasp.

04:53.800 --> 04:54.690
Understood.

04:55.440 --> 04:57.570
We'll stay here and buy you time.

04:59.820 --> 05:02.620
And I'll get the meteor in the meantime.

05:02.620 --> 05:03.950
Think you'll last?

05:03.950 --> 05:07.290
I'd say that depends on
how fast you are.

05:07.630 --> 05:09.830
Alright, you're on.

05:09.830 --> 05:12.670
I'll leave Gaston with you.
Use him well.

05:12.670 --> 05:13.880
I'm stayin' too?!

05:16.700 --> 05:20.010
We're surprised to see
you can entertain us,

05:20.010 --> 05:24.010
but a bunch of water lizards
simply won't do.

05:24.600 --> 05:29.350
A gourmet like us has standards
for appetizers!

05:29.350 --> 05:30.180
Gaston!

05:30.180 --> 05:33.060
If I die here,
I'm comin' back to haunt you!

05:39.430 --> 05:41.450
Don't get in the way—

05:42.910 --> 05:44.810
Mana Flow, eh?

05:44.810 --> 05:47.410
Not bad for a lumbering oaf.

05:47.410 --> 05:50.160
Who you callin' an oaf?!

05:53.460 --> 05:56.630
Oho, we see.

05:56.630 --> 05:59.800
So it was that sort of plan.

06:01.760 --> 06:06.650
You seem calm for someone
who's fumbled everything so far.

06:09.020 --> 06:11.730
With that girl gone,

06:11.730 --> 06:15.060
guess that's three Rui would like.

06:17.900 --> 06:22.240
This past year, I've been thrown into
more fights than the average grunt.

06:22.240 --> 06:25.200
I wonder what kind of merchant
that makes me.

06:44.840 --> 06:48.390
Damn, that's gross.

06:48.390 --> 06:51.180
I've never been good
with gory stuff.

06:53.060 --> 06:55.690
Calling a lady gross?

06:55.690 --> 06:58.810
You'll never get any girls
if you can't dress up your words.

06:59.230 --> 07:04.070
Or is that just how it is with guys
who love sneaking in the shadows?

07:04.650 --> 07:05.400
What?

07:05.950 --> 07:09.410
You know, I've been thinking

07:09.410 --> 07:13.120
about which asshole
opened the watergate

07:13.120 --> 07:16.330
and flooded half of this city.

07:16.720 --> 07:18.330
If it weren't for that,

07:18.330 --> 07:23.340
we'd have everything
we wanted by now.

07:25.720 --> 07:28.760
Can't say I know
what you're talking about.

07:29.160 --> 07:31.060
On~top~of~that...

07:31.060 --> 07:36.520
You know those assholes who knew
where the Witch's bones were?

07:36.520 --> 07:42.440
They all just dropped dead
without me doing anything.

07:42.440 --> 07:45.150
Well, that's unfortunate.

07:45.150 --> 07:48.950
In a mess like this,
bad luck can hit you from anywhere.

07:50.120 --> 07:52.490
Playing dumb?

07:52.490 --> 07:54.080
It's okay.

07:54.080 --> 08:00.540
My sublime love will take in
even the likes of you.

08:01.250 --> 08:04.380
As long as you take off that helmet,
show me your face,

08:04.380 --> 08:07.300
take me to bed,
and make love with me, that is.

08:08.930 --> 08:09.930
Sorry.

08:10.510 --> 08:12.260
I appreciate the thought,

08:12.260 --> 08:15.060
but we don't know each other
that well yet.

08:15.560 --> 08:18.560
Plus, it'd be awkward
if my friends started gossiping,

08:18.560 --> 08:20.310
so I'll have to decline.

08:20.730 --> 08:26.400
I see, a masochist who loves being
tossed around by women.

08:26.400 --> 08:29.950
I don't really dislike
your kind of man-meat.

08:29.950 --> 08:31.660
Huh? The hell are you—

08:31.660 --> 08:35.290
Has a sharp gaze
and a voluptuous body.

08:35.290 --> 08:38.540
Arrogant, moody,

08:38.540 --> 08:41.250
talks a lot, but smart.

08:41.250 --> 08:43.210
Something like this?

08:43.210 --> 08:45.670
As for the hair length...

08:45.670 --> 08:48.880
Whoops, not blonde, I guess.

08:48.880 --> 08:51.620
Red, maybe?

08:51.620 --> 08:53.430
No, it's orange.

08:53.770 --> 08:57.520
Her age should be... around here.

08:59.480 --> 09:01.310
How's my voice?

09:01.310 --> 09:04.570
Tch, you make me sick.

09:05.020 --> 09:07.440
Where the hell did you see
the Princess?

09:07.440 --> 09:11.030
Never seen her or heard of her before
in my life.

09:11.030 --> 09:13.490
I can't see your face,

09:13.490 --> 09:15.330
but your reactions,
your attitude...

09:15.700 --> 09:21.040
Any move you make, I won't miss.
I'm the type who gives it my all.

09:21.040 --> 09:23.080
So look at me.

09:23.080 --> 09:25.130
Look only at me!

09:25.840 --> 09:28.050
My face, my body,
my voice, my gestures...

09:28.050 --> 09:30.090
Everything, every last bit of me...

09:30.500 --> 09:33.840
is supposed to be exactly
what you're into, damn it!

09:36.180 --> 09:40.940
Sorry, but this world ain't ready
for that kind of love yet.

09:40.940 --> 09:43.980
Why do you reject me?

09:43.980 --> 09:48.150
What exactly is it about me
that you don't like?

09:48.150 --> 09:50.150
Don't get me wrong.

09:50.150 --> 09:52.950
I don't love you or hate you.

09:52.950 --> 09:54.070
I couldn't care less.

09:55.240 --> 09:56.490
Sorry, I lied.

09:56.990 --> 10:00.500
You're disgusting, and so, I hate you.

10:00.500 --> 10:02.710
It hurts to even look at you.

10:03.830 --> 10:07.630
You unfaithful piece of rotten meat!

10:13.510 --> 10:14.510
Dona!

10:27.940 --> 10:32.040
Turn into muddy fireworks, El Dona!

10:44.500 --> 10:46.210
How's that? That oughta be—

10:46.210 --> 10:48.420
Oh, you're so horrible!

10:50.390 --> 10:51.170
Shit.

10:51.630 --> 10:55.670
You didn't have to go that far.

10:56.510 --> 10:59.010
Now that's just cheating.

10:59.010 --> 11:00.470
Oh my~!

11:00.470 --> 11:03.020
You don't back down
even when things get tough!

11:03.020 --> 11:05.190
How brave!

11:05.190 --> 11:07.480
My love for you
just went through the roof!

11:09.020 --> 11:12.440
Sorry, but the Princess
smacked me on the ass

11:12.440 --> 11:14.360
and told me
to take care of things here.

11:14.360 --> 11:17.280
Sure, a squiggly shape-shifting
woman like you is scary,

11:17.280 --> 11:21.080
but ruining the Princess' mood
is worse.

11:21.080 --> 11:24.830
Talking about another woman
in front of me again?

11:24.830 --> 11:30.790
Looks like I'm really going to
take my time correcting you.

11:30.790 --> 11:32.880
Agh, damn it.

11:33.380 --> 11:36.290
My stars are so bad today.

11:46.770 --> 11:48.310
Where...

12:00.740 --> 12:05.160
So, what kind of guy
is this Eight-Arms Kurgan?

12:05.750 --> 12:09.790
Frankly speakin', he's a livin' legend.

12:10.250 --> 12:11.500
A legend?

12:11.500 --> 12:12.500
Yeah.

12:13.050 --> 12:18.260
Us demi-humans have
a high affinity for magic,

12:18.260 --> 12:22.350
except for the many-armed tribe.

12:23.120 --> 12:28.230
Despite the other tribes securing a stable place
for themselves in the Vollachia Empire,

12:28.230 --> 12:31.020
the many-armed tribe was mocked
and discriminated against.

12:31.520 --> 12:33.940
Then Kurgan came in
and turned the tables.

12:34.650 --> 12:37.820
Some lord tried to wipe 'em out,

12:37.820 --> 12:41.200
but Kurgan single-handedly wiped out
that lord's soldiers instead,

12:41.200 --> 12:43.780
and forced him to recognize his tribe.

12:44.450 --> 12:49.580
Unlike most of the many-armed race
who were born with four to five arms,

12:50.080 --> 12:52.670
Kurgan was born with eight.

12:52.670 --> 12:55.090
I heard that from a young age,

12:55.090 --> 12:58.470
he was seen as odd and ostracized
even within his own tribe.

12:59.010 --> 13:02.430
Despite that, he took up the sword
for the sake of his people.

13:02.430 --> 13:05.140
You mean Devil Cleavers.

13:05.510 --> 13:06.430
Indeed.

13:06.890 --> 13:10.390
Kurgan wields multiple swords
known as Devil Cleavers.

13:10.890 --> 13:14.650
However, he only draws them
against those he acknowledges.

13:15.110 --> 13:17.860
Having him unsheathe
all his Devil Cleavers

13:17.860 --> 13:21.610
is considered a mark of
a warrior's acclaim.

13:21.610 --> 13:26.200
In short,
he's still treatin' me like a kid.

13:55.020 --> 13:57.110
Don'th undereshtimate mhe!

15:14.480 --> 15:16.310
A shelter?

15:17.190 --> 15:18.690
How did I...

15:18.690 --> 15:20.150
Gorgeous Tiger?

15:30.990 --> 15:32.790
Gorgeous Tiger...

16:12.910 --> 16:16.790
I love you, Garfiel Tinsel.

16:17.540 --> 16:20.990
Well, I don't.

16:21.790 --> 16:24.050
And you're not her.

16:38.480 --> 16:40.770
Th-Thank you.

16:45.280 --> 16:46.490
Get away.

17:00.210 --> 17:02.030
Gorgeous Tiger!

17:02.670 --> 17:04.000
Gorgeous Tiger!

17:04.000 --> 17:05.670
Hey, kid.

17:05.670 --> 17:06.520
What're ya...

17:06.520 --> 17:08.420
Gorgeous Tiger!

17:08.420 --> 17:11.430
G-Gorgeous Tiger!

17:11.430 --> 17:14.180
- Just sit tight and don't worry about—
- Gorgeous Tiger!

17:14.680 --> 17:15.930
Please win!

17:15.930 --> 17:17.470
Gorgeous Tiger!

17:17.470 --> 17:19.640
All we can do is watch, but still...!

17:19.640 --> 17:21.520
- Fight and win!
- C'mon, you're goin' overboard.

17:21.520 --> 17:23.230
Tiger! You can do it!

17:26.570 --> 17:31.490
Looks like your speech worked
a little too well, Chief.

17:32.950 --> 17:34.410
Sorry 'bout 'em.

17:34.410 --> 17:37.880
It's gettin' too loud for a duel.

17:38.290 --> 17:40.250
Especially those two.

17:40.720 --> 17:44.290
They're my lil bro and lil sis.

17:44.680 --> 17:47.960
I'll give 'em a good talkin'-to after this.

17:47.960 --> 17:49.010
You can do it!

17:52.680 --> 17:55.240
You can do it, Gorgeous Tiger!

18:17.740 --> 18:19.620
Thanks.

18:19.620 --> 18:20.860
I'm...

18:25.540 --> 18:30.710
I'm the ultimate shield, no...

18:30.710 --> 18:34.840
Garfiel Tinsel, the Gorgeous Tiger!

20:28.290 --> 20:29.730
Magnificent.

20:30.960 --> 20:34.960
A WARRIOR'S ACCLAIM

22:09.600 --> 22:12.860
There was nothin' heroic about that.

22:13.520 --> 22:15.440
Gorgeous Tiger...

22:19.400 --> 22:21.400
Don't go cryin' over me.

22:21.950 --> 22:24.780
D-Dummy!

22:24.780 --> 22:27.370
I'm not crying.

22:27.910 --> 22:29.940
Just get some rest!

22:30.500 --> 22:34.000
We'll get a healer quick.

22:34.000 --> 22:36.000
Oh crap, not good.

22:37.340 --> 22:38.340
Gorgeous Tiger!

22:39.750 --> 22:41.170
Gorgeous Tiger!

22:41.170 --> 22:43.550
- Hang in there!
- Someone call a healer!

22:43.550 --> 22:45.800
- Gorgeous Tiger?!
- Someone, help!

22:45.800 --> 22:49.100
I wonder... if they're doin' alright.

22:59.820 --> 23:02.070
The Reaper's Divine Protection.

23:02.530 --> 23:06.530
I'd never have guessed
I could fight for this long.

23:07.240 --> 23:09.410
I chose this path under no delusion,

23:10.290 --> 23:13.000
and I hold no hope
for divine intervention.

23:13.460 --> 23:16.710
We'll have plenty of time to enjoy
ourselves in the heavens above.

23:17.750 --> 23:19.670
I will not dream.

23:20.340 --> 23:21.880
This is reality.

23:22.800 --> 23:26.340
Theresia, you are beautiful.

23:27.550 --> 23:30.560
That is why you shouldn't be here!
